        "original_id": "f7097a64-1225-5b30-ad9b-0f23f707d36a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Crown Jewels, A Night at the Opera\n- People: Queen, Marx Brothers\n- Companies: EMI Records, Elektra Records\n- Topics: album packaging, album naming\n\nFacts:\n- A Night at the Opera is the fourth studio album by Queen.\n- A Night at the Opera was released on 21 November 1975 by EMI Records in the United Kingdom and by Elektra Records in the United States.\n- Queen named A Night at the Opera after the Marx Brothers film of the same name, which the band watched during recording at the studio complex.\n- The Crown Jewels is a box set by Queen.\n- The Crown Jewels comprises Queen's first eight studio albums: Queen, Queen II, Sheer Heart Attack, A Night at the Opera, A Day at the Races, News of the World, Jazz, and The Game.\n- The albums in The Crown Jewels are presented in sleeves that replicate the original vinyl packaging.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "20c022c2-ba17-5ed3-904b-0dd9a2e1d9b6",
